# Git already stores every text file in this repository with LF. What differs
# is the checkout: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, files arrive with CRLF,
# and Prettier — configured endOfLine "lf" — then reports them as malformatted.
# Before this file, `pnpm format:check` failed on 104 files locally while the
# identical CI step passed on Linux, which trained everyone to ignore it.
#
# eol=lf pins the checkout, so the working tree matches what is stored and what
# CI sees, regardless of a contributor's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted. text=auto detects most of
# these, but favicon.ico contains CR bytes and is the one file in the tree that
# a heuristic could plausibly misread, so the rules are explicit.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
